/// **Six totals over a whole tree cancel.** [`EXCUSED`] is a count per *marker*,
/// so a hatch written onto a live dangling citation and one taken off a line of
/// prose leave every printed number and every row of that list byte-identical —
/// and the first of those is a gate switched off for a real defect while the
/// second is nothing at all. A count per file does not cancel across files,
/// which is the move the totals cannot see.
///
/// The rows are the *places*, and most of them are fixtures: `wall.rs` feeds its
/// own gate the call sites it must refuse, and each of those is a marked line in
/// a string literal. That is why this is a written-down list rather than a rule
/// — it says where the hatches are, and never that any of them is earned.
#[cfg(test)]
